label scenario_4a:
    
    "You and Gavyn are on a walk. You plan on heading back in a few minutes 
    because it's starting to get dark."

    "\"Can I show you this song I've been into?\" he asks as you turn the corner 
    to an unfamiliar part of campus." 

    "You agree to listen, putting in one headphone of his wired earbuds."

    "It's a soft warm love song with lyrics like \"I don't know what I'll do if you leave\" 
    and \"You're the only one I need.\""
    
    "The song is nice, but your heart sinks a little with each new line."
    
    "When the song is over, he turns to you."
    
    "\"So… What did you think?\""

    menu:
        "\"It was great! I loved the melody.\"":
            jump loved_melody

        "\"Not really my taste, I think\"":
            jump not_my_taste

        "\"Why'd you play this for me?\"":
            jump why_play

        "\"The words are a bit intense...\"":
            jump intense_words

label loved_melody:

    "Gavyn smiles softly and tells you he's really glad you enjoyed it."

    "He often asks to go on more walks, showing you more songs like this one, 
    taking you to similarly remote spots when he does so."

# not quite my tempo
label not_my_taste:

    "His face drops a little and he seems a bit hurt. He plays it off like he's fine, 
    poking fun at you for simply having bad taste."

    "Whenever you two discuss a matter of opinion from now on, he half-playfully states 
    you have no right to speak on account of your \"bad taste.\""

label why_play:

    "He seems dejected. \"I just wanted to show you something I liked. 
    It really speaks to how I feel about love.\""

label intense_words:

    "His eyes light up. \"I know, right? It really encapsulates what love feels like for me...
    especially when I'm not sure if the other person likes me back.\""

    "When he discovers new songs now, he sends them to you and tries to start up a conversation about the lyrics."
